* Single battery port. P, N are the battery rail. H, L are the DC-link rail.
* D is signed phase shift as a fraction of HALF a switching period.
* Positive D = discharge into the link. Stiff external DC rails are required.
.subckt DAB P N H L params: D=0.16 FSW=50k NSEC=14 LK=1.5u LM=180u RP=3m RLO=1m RHI=35m DT=120n STOP=1e9 IMAG0=0
.param TPER={1/FSW} EDGE=25n
.param TPRI={max(-D,0)*TPER/2} TSEC={max(D,0)*TPER/2}

* Isolated ideal gate commands, with both diagonals off during dead time.
VPA rawpa N PULSE(0 5 {TPRI+DT/2} {EDGE} {EDGE} {TPER/2-DT-EDGE} {TPER})
VPB rawpb N PULSE(0 5 {TPRI+TPER/2+DT/2} {EDGE} {EDGE} {TPER/2-DT-EDGE} {TPER})
VSA rawsa L PULSE(0 5 {TSEC+DT/2} {EDGE} {EDGE} {TPER/2-DT-EDGE} {TPER})
VSB rawsb L PULSE(0 5 {TSEC+TPER/2+DT/2} {EDGE} {EDGE} {TPER/2-DT-EDGE} {TPER})
* Command inhibition only. Body diodes remain present when both bridges stop.
Ben en N V={max(0,min(1,(STOP-time)/EDGE))}
Bpa cpa N V={v(rawpa,N)*v(en,N)}
Bpb cpb N V={v(rawpb,N)*v(en,N)}
Bsa csa L V={v(rawsa,L)*v(en,N)}
Bsb csb L V={v(rawsb,L)*v(en,N)}

.include dab-power.inc
.ends DAB
